      "message": "Yes, it is intentional. Added comment to L.2442\n\nIt is a preparation to test the case#6 (wifi upstream removes tethering information) on T- device. \n\nFor U+ devices, case#5 (xlat offload) adds tethering information. we don\u0027t need to that preparation (l.2361).\n\nref:\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/2174904/23/Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java#2358\n```\n// Test case:\n// - Clat offload is supported on U+ devices.\n// +-------+-------+-----------------------+\n// | Test  | Up    |       Protocol        |\n// | Case# | stream+-------+-------+-------+\n// |       |       | IPv4  | IPv6  | Xlat  |\n// +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+\n// |   1   | Cell  |   O   |       |       |\n// +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+\n// |   2   | Cell  |       |   O   |       |\n// +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+\n// |   3   | Cell  |   O   |   O   |       |\n// +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+\n// |   4   |   -   |       |       |       |\n// +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+\n// |   5   | Cell  |       |   O   |   O   |\n// +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+\n// |   6   | Wifi  |   O   |   O   |       | \u003c-- doesn\u0027t support offload (ether ip)\n// +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+\n```",
